WEBVTT

00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:14,500
Can you please explain how blood plasma transfusions work?

00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:18,300
Are they good for cancer patients?

00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:24,700
So well, there is a difference in whether if you're

00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:33,940
doing a blood transfusion for low red blood cells

00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:37,260
then you're going to do a whole blood transfusion.

00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:41,660
Or you're going to do packed red blood cell transfusion

00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:45,340
to help with anidemia.

00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:49,580
That would be common with a person with cancer

00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:52,380
if they have anidemia.

00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:56,540
So they have greatly reduced hemoglobin.

00:00:56,540 --> 00:00:59,540
Usually that is the deciding factor

00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:02,700
and whether they're going to get a transfusion or not.

00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:05,180
You won't get just a straight plasma transfusion.

00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:10,060
You get a full blood transfusion or packed red blood cell transfusion.

00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:13,740
The negative about getting just a plasma transfusion,

00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:16,260
it can be a negative with any blood transfusion

00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:21,060
is that you can develop an immune reaction to it.

00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:24,340
Not that you're getting the wrong type of blood,

00:01:24,340 --> 00:01:26,300
but that you are getting different blood

00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:28,140
and it can contain antibodies.

00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:31,420
And it can spark an immune reaction, which

00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:34,540
can take away from your immune system's ability

00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:35,420
if I cancer.

00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:40,380
So it's not recommended to get something

00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:42,060
unless you absolutely need it.

00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:44,940
But you're typically not going to get

00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,740
a recommendation of a blood transfusion

00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:52,820
unless your hemoglobin is 7.5% below.

00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:56,540
So it wouldn't even be in the cards.

00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:59,300
But certainly, if your hemoglobin is that low,

00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:03,420
the clinic or transfusion is most likely

00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:05,580
that it's really the best thing to do,

00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:09,500
whether you can function, you can keep it over

00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:10,420
as long as that.

00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:12,900
You're going to have a lot of irregularities

00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:15,380
for signs and symptoms.

00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:23,280
And I highly recommend it to give transfusion.

00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:28,120
But you can't have negative outcomes of getting a transfusion.

00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:32,440
It could also be fun, especially as a person

00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:37,800
has a core of entity of an immune reaction too.

00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,000
So you got to do it.

